# Initial66 literal context and documentary bootstrap

Root authority: ROOT_GO66_INITIAL_CONTEXT_ONLY.json, creator6482857252;
published proper contracts263b9d4329043e6debd299a8c27327ee515670d7.
This plan implements only the already adopted SPEC/PLAN's context/custody
step. It does not activate proof text or mathematical execution.

1. Write dedicated66 capture/worker/bootstrap scripts, initial source header
   and complete FROZEN_CONTEXT.md before the first documentary worker.
2. Invoke the dedicated entry capture, dedicated outer capture, then actual
   documentary record_run worker, then bootstrap_context.py. Preserve each
   command/cwd/time/status and separate original stdout/stderr.
3. Worker FIRST-hashes only necessary new versions once, seeds the copied
   controls with root's known ID, and makes exact text snapshots with reused
   IDs before launching the child. It never snapshots or copies objects.
4. Bootstrap binds those cached IDs in INITIAL_CONTEXT_FREEZE.json; it
   performs no Lean/API probe, proof edit, fixture/harness body or old hash.
5. Deliver the complete literal context and closed actual capture paths to
   root for FULL reading/acceptance. Await separate applicable TEXT release.

No tests of unchanged mathematics or runner replay are planned. The actual
documentary bootstrap is the necessary first exercise of this new runner;
any concrete defect will be preserved and corrected narrowly with full
actual patch/history before another authorized invocation. A failed inner
worker and failed outer/entry return remain distinct observed records.
